// Non-empty on purpose: frappe.desk.query_report.get_script() falls
// back to `"frappe.query_reports['{}']={{}}".format(report_name)` when a
// report has neither a .js file nor this field set. That .format() call
// doesn't escape the apostrophe in "Today's Departures", so the generated
// script breaks out of its JS string literal early and the browser throws
// `SyntaxError: Unexpected identifier 's'`, aborting the whole report page
// (blank -- no title, filters, or columns render). Setting any truthy
// javascript here skips that fallback branch entirely.
